    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023\n1. Preliminary\nTitle, Commencement, and Application: Applies to all persons in India and beyond under specific conditions.\n2. Summary Trials\nEligible Offences: Not punishable by death, life imprisonment, or imprisonment over 3 years.\nProcedure:\nMagistrate's Powers: Try summarily with the accused's opportunity to be heard.\nRecord and Judgment: In the language of the Court, with substance of evidence and brief reasons.\n3. Punishments for Offences \n•\tCognizable, Non-Bailable, Non-Compoundable:\n•\tUnfair Means in Exams: 3-5 years’ imprisonment, up to ₹10 lakh fine.\n•\tService Providers: Up to ₹1 crore fine, 4-year ban from exam responsibilities.\n•\tSenior Management Involvement: 3-10 years’ imprisonment, ₹1 crore fine.\n4. Other Procedural Aspects \nArrest and Summons Procedures\nPowers of Police and Magistrates\nPublic Responsibilities",
